---
description: Hard boundaries around generated C++ code.
globs: ["engine/generated/**/*", "apps/orchestrator/**/pipeline/**/*"]
alwaysApply: true
---

# Generated-code boundaries

- Generated C++ (`.cpp`, `.h`, `.hpp`) may only live under:
  - `engine/generated/mechanics/`
  - `engine/generated/ai/`
  - `engine/generated/dialogue/`
  - `engine/generated/world/` (VR environment builders)
- Generated code MUST implement one of the abstract interfaces in
  `engine/runtime/include/ptv/api/`:
  - `IMechanic` for gameplay mechanics.
  - `IBehaviour` for NPC / AI behavior, overriding the context-taking
   `on_attach(..., MechanicContext&)` / `on_tick(..., const InputSnapshot&,
   MechanicContext&)` (the engine hosts behaviours like mechanics; the
   context-free forms are legacy and rejected for new code).
  - `IDialogueHook` for dialogue logic.
  - `IWorldBuilder` for VR environment generation (world/ only).
- Generated files register themselves with `PTV_REGISTER_MECHANIC("id")` (or
  the sibling macros `PTV_REGISTER_BEHAVIOUR`, `PTV_REGISTER_DIALOGUE_HOOK`,
  `PTV_REGISTER_WORLD_BUILDER`). They never modify `MechanicRegistry`, the
  renderer, the XR session loop, the platform layer, memory management, or the
  ECS core.
- World builders (`engine/generated/world/`) have a TIGHTER include whitelist:
  only `ptv/api/IWorldBuilder.h`, the C++ standard library, and `<glm/...>`.
  They may NOT include ECS (`entt`, `ptv/ecs/`), `nlohmann`, or any other
  engine header. They are compiled + run OFFLINE in the `ptv_worldgen` host
  (which links no Vulkan/OpenXR/Jolt/renderer/ECS) and only emit `scene.json`.
- Generated header files (`.h`/`.hpp`) are allowed under the same directories
  as `.cpp` files, subject to the same include whitelist. They are for
  task-local helpers, structs, and shared declarations only.
- Generated headers may be included via bare filename (`#include "foo.h"`)
 by files in the SAME task, or by a task that declares the owning task in
 its `depends_on` (both live in the same project directory and the
 dependency is built first — e.g. a weapon profile that
 `depends_on: ["shooting_hub"]` may `#include "shooting_hub_shared.h"`).
 Including a header from a task that is neither the same task nor a
 declared dependency, or from another project, is forbidden.
- Registration macros (`PTV_REGISTER_MECHANIC`, `PTV_REGISTER_BEHAVIOUR`,
  `PTV_REGISTER_DIALOGUE_HOOK`, `PTV_REGISTER_WORLD_BUILDER`) must only appear
  in `.cpp` files, never in headers.
- Generated files must not include engine internals other than the public
  `ptv/api/*` headers and the public scene / ECS headers.
- The orchestrator validates includes before writing files (fail-loudly)
  and `engine/tools/check_generated_bounds.py` runs before the build as a
  secondary check, failing the stage on any violation.
